{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 56, :comments ["<b>And the famine was over all the face of the land, and Joseph opened all the storehouses</b>: He says that Joseph did not open what was stored with them until the famine grew strong in the land — not as when they cried out to Pharaoh immediately, for people cry out when they still have a little sustenance, and he wanted nothing at all to remain to them. This is the meaning of \"and the famine was over all the face of the land\" (Genesis 41:56), for before he opened his storehouses the famine was over all the face of the land. And he further returned to explain that he did not sell to them until it grew very strong upon them. Or perhaps Scripture intensifies to say that it was a famine of utter devastation."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:43:39.633084741Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}